I checked the added neighbors against public records. The revised positioning is substantially fixed.

1. **Missing CRC/recsys/ranking neighbors:** Adequately addressed. De Toni et al. are correctly positioned as CRC for unwanted recommendations, not rank-quality selective reliability; their abstract explicitly frames bounding unwanted content in personalized recommendation ([arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.16829)). Guo et al. are fairly described as stochastic LTR with finite-sample utility/fairness risk control ([arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.07188)). Intrator et al. are correctly conformal IR / score-refinement retrieval sets ([ACL](https://aclanthology.org/2024.fever-1.22/)). Xu et al. are correctly elevated as the serious nDCG-like ranked-retrieval risk-control neighbor ([IJCAI](https://www.ijcai.org/proceedings/2025/1012)).

2. **Angelopoulos 2023 correction:** Adequately addressed. The text now says FDR / “mostly good” returned sets plus diversity, matching the paper’s abstract and not the earlier size/coverage mischaracterization ([arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/2207.01609)).

3. **Distinction from listwise NDCG / Xu 2025:** Adequately addressed. The revision explicitly concedes that “NDCG” is not the novelty and moves the claim to post-abstention conditional served-slice risk with random served count plus frozen-lambda B1/B2 discipline. That is the right separation from Xu’s all-query/stage-wise control.

4. **“To our knowledge” de-stacking:** Mostly addressed. The novelty is now stated conceptually, not as a fragile priority claim. I would still delete the meta “citation-audit / Codex review” paragraph from paper-facing text.

**Remaining reviewer objection:** the guarantee wording still needs mathematical tightening. “`E[1−NDCG@k | served]` is bounded by α in marginal expectation” is easy to misread: specify the randomness, zero/low-served-count handling, coverage floor, and whether the certificate is over the accepted-law mean, B2 empirical mean, or a numerator-plus-coverage surrogate. This is a formal-positioning issue, not an experiment request.

SCORE_POSITIONING: 8.2/10.
